  "name": "Plant care",
  "publisher": "Initiative",
  "description": "Every plant watered before it wilts, and not so often that it drowns.",
  "long_description": "Each plant gets its own jobs: watering, fertilizing and repotting, each a type with a page of its own. Watering and fertilizing repeat from when you last did them, not from a calendar, so a week away does not leave you three waterings behind.\n\nEvery job says which plant, which room and how much light it gets. The table opens grouped by room, which is the order you walk round the house in. A plant that looks unwell goes in Needs a look until somebody works out what it wants.\n\nRepotting starts with a checklist, because the step everyone skips is the week out of direct sun afterwards.",
